{"name":"Smiley Face","hex":"#ffc962","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smiley face","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smiley, a simplified drawing of a smiling face, using two dots for the eyes and an arc for the mouth.","A smiley, a sequence of text characters used to represent a happy mood, e.g. :) or :-)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smiley_face"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smiley","blocks":[{"text":"A smiley, also known as a smiley face, is a basic ideogram representing a smiling face. Since the 1950s, it has become part of popular culture worldwide, used either as a standalone ideogram or as a form of communication, such as emoticons. The smiley began as two dots and a line representing eyes and a mouth. More elaborate designs emerged in the 1950s, featuring noses, eyebrows, and outlines. New York radio station WMCA used a yellow and black design for its \"Good Guys!\" campaign in the early 1960s. More yellow-and-black designs appeared in the 1960s and 1970s, including works by Harvey Ross Ball in 1963, and Franklin Loufrani in 1971. The Smiley Company, founded by Franklin Loufrani, claims to hold the rights to a version of the smiley face in over 100 countries. It has become one of the top 100 licensing companies globally."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Smiley.svg/330px-Smiley.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smiley","wikidata":"Q11241"},{"title":"Smiley Face (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Smiley Face is a 2007 stoner comedy film directed and co-produced by Gregg Araki. Written by Dylan Haggerty, it stars Anna Faris as a young woman who has a series of misadventures after eating cupcakes laced with cannabis. The supporting cast includes Danny Masterson, Adam Brody, Rick Hoffman, Jane Lynch, John Krasinski, Marion Ross, Michael Hitchcock, John Cho, Danny Trejo, and Roscoe Lee Browne in his final film appearance. Smiley Face was the ninth feature film directed by Araki."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0a/Smiley_facemp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smiley_Face_(film)","wikidata":"Q959483"},{"title":"Face","blocks":[{"text":"The face is \"the front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose and mouth, and the surrounding area.\" While that basic structure is found in many animals, the evolutionary development of mammals has led to a wide diversity of facial types between those species, identifiable by characteristics of facial features and expressive behaviors."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Human_faces.jpg/330px-Human_faces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Face","wikidata":"Q37017"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Smiley_1741_Hennet.jpg/500px-Smiley_1741_Hennet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d6/Smiley_1741_Hennet.jpg/500px-Smiley_1741_Hennet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmiley_1741_Hennet.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Smiley_Regensburg_3.jpg/330px-Smiley_Regensburg_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Smiley_Regensburg_3.jpg/330px-Smiley_Regensburg_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmiley_Regensburg_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Erwin_Schulhoff_-_In_Futurum_-_rests_%28o